From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:55:35 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: vc1: pad the OUTPUT buffers, not the format

The 16 KiB of slack the VC-1 bit reader needs past the end of a frame
was added to sizeimage each time the OUTPUT format was prepared, so
TRY_FMT and S_FMT with the format G_FMT returned grew it by 16 KiB
again, and negotiating the format did not converge.

Keep sizeimage as negotiated and add the slack to the size of the
buffers allocated for the VC-1 OUTPUT queue instead.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c   | 17 +++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
index 0e87f24f6..b6606af5f 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -228,14 +228,6 @@ void cedrus_prepare_format(struct v4l2_pix_format *pix_fmt,
 		bytesperline = 0;
 		/* Choose some minimum size since this can't be 0 */
 		sizeimage = max_t(u32, SZ_1K, sizeimage);
-		/*
-		 * VC-1 over-reads the bitstream a little past the end of a frame
-		 * on the last macroblock; pad the source allocation so the bit
-		 * reader has slack and the DMA does not stall (see
-		 * cedrus_vc1_setup()).
-		 */
-		if (pix_fmt->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VC1_SLICE)
-			sizeimage += SZ_16K;
 		/* The VP9 bitstream end address has a 1 KiB granularity. */
 		if (pix_fmt->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME)
 			sizeimage = ALIGN(sizeimage, SZ_1K);
@@ -897,6 +889,15 @@ static int cedrus_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *vq, unsigned int *nbufs,
 			return -EINVAL;
 	} else {
 		sizes[0] = pix_fmt->sizeimage;
+		/*
+		 * VC-1 over-reads the bitstream a little past the end of a
+		 * frame on the last macroblock; pad the source allocation so
+		 * the bit reader has slack and the DMA does not stall (see
+		 * cedrus_vc1_setup()).
+		 */
+		if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(vq->type) &&
+		    pix_fmt->pixelformat == V4L2_PIX_FMT_VC1_SLICE)
+			sizes[0] += SZ_16K;
 		*nplanes = 1;
 	}
 
